Z||000000||AusFiero||06-02-2001||10:47 AM||||I noticed stateside everyone, that is into them anyway, drives these huge truck like pickups as apposed to in Australia where the ute is considered the normal work truck/recreational vehicle.<P>Difference, yours are bloody big. Ours are much smaller and car based not unlike your elcaminoes (do they still make them?).<P>Anyway here is a picture of General Motors Holden's latest concept. Based on a VX HSV (Holden Special Vehicles) which comes standard with a 300KW 5.7 ltr V8, 6 speed manual or 4 speed auto, body kit, tuned suspensions, 4 wheel discs, 18X8 alloys and a list of features longer than your arm. Not your average work truck you might say  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>The additions on this vehicle to make it a concept vehicle is only the glass removable roof and a wind down rear window with a slightly different interior.<P>Thought I may as well post it as I am sure you wouldn't see too many Australian cars without searching for them.<P><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/vxute01_2.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/fiero.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A><BR>When I was young I spent 80% of my money on Women, Gambling and Alcohol. I guess I wasted the rest.||||reg||6
Z||000001||LZeitgeist||06-02-2001||10:57 AM||||That's pretty sweet-looking...!<P><BR>AusFiero... whenever your .sig pic is on my screen, my mouse pointer moves slowly and jerkily, and seems to get stuck every other second, but when I scroll past your pic so it's not showing on my screen anymore, my mouse works normally again...<P>Does anyone else have the same trouble? <P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||AusFiero||06-02-2001||11:09 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by LZeitgeist:<BR><B><BR>AusFiero... whenever your .sig pic is on my screen, my mouse pointer moves slowly and jerkily, and seems to get stuck every other second, but when I scroll past your pic so it's not showing on my screen anymore, my mouse works normally again...<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>What sort of PC are you running (CPU speed) and more importantly how much memory and video memory?<P>||||reg||1
