Z||000006||LZeitgeist||06-02-2001||11:30 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>What sort of PC are you running (CPU speed) and more importantly how much memory and video memory?<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hewlett Packard Pentium II, 450mHz with a 100mHz bus, 96 Meg of RAM, 2 Meg video RAM...<P>Your .sig file is the first (and so far, only) graphic I've had this particular problem with - I was just curious what may be different about it.||||reg||1
Z||000007||AusFiero||06-02-2001||11:47 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by TRiAD:<BR><B>How much is a new VX HSV these days?<BR>Used to be around $25KUS, LT1, 6sp, RWD, 4dr...*drooooool*<BR>God, I LOVE Holdens!<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well that has changed somewhat with the newer models, as have the goodies packed into them though.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>For new HSV vehicles you have the following with close approximate pricing as they vary so much with many options available.<P>HSV Commodore XU6 - Supercharged V6 power auto or 5 speed - US$25K<BR>HSV Commodore models from R8 to Senator and others range in price from around US$30K to around US$36K with various V8 engine and horsepower output options. 5.0 ltr  or 5.7 ltr.<BR>Top of the line HSV GTS with 300kw and 6 speed etc etc etc is US$45K to US$55K Can get it supercharged from HSV as well to give it about 380kw off the showroom floor. That costs more again.<P>Next year they are re-releasing our long lost seventies muscle car icon the Holden Monaro Coupe (based on the 4 door Commodore but with a new roofline and 1/4s). It will come only as a top of the line HSV GTS it appears and will be priced around US$55K. It is also rumoured to be the replacement platform for the soon to die USA GM F-Body series. <P>A well known Pontiac personality from the GTO era also owns a HSV GTS that resides in San Diego. So if you live around that way keep an eye out.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000008||AusFiero||06-02-2001||11:55 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by LZeitgeist:<BR><B> Hewlett Packard Pentium II, 450mHz with a 100mHz bus, 96 Meg of RAM, 2 Meg video RAM...<P>Your .sig file is the first (and so far, only) graphic I've had this particular problem with - I was just curious what may be different about it.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>It is a Macromedia Flash movie exported as an animated gif. How does your pute handle Flash sites? <BR>It is probably the 2 meg of video ram that is a problem as I haven't even seen anything under 16 meg and upwards ones for a couple of years now. How many applications you have open can change things too. Also do you have any memory resident programs running in the background that require video ram? <P>Anyone else with smaller vidoe cards having problems?<P>Looks like back to the drawing board to tone it down a little.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000009||btoth||06-02-2001||06:51 PM||||2meg of video ram?  What's a computer that fast doing with only 2mb of video ram?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000010||Raydar||06-02-2001||09:00 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by TRiAD:<BR><B> Heck, GM should just sell Holdens here!<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I agree completely! <BR>Every so often, I'll drift over to the Holden site, and look, and drool.<BR>If GM sold the Commodore SS here, people would be lining up at the boat for them.<BR>Haven't seen any pics of the Monaro, yet.<BR>I saw the Ute on Holden's site, yesterday. Was thinking how much it resembled an ElCamino. On Steroids.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Aus, There haven't been any new El Caminos since late 80's, early 90's, I guess. <P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 06-02-2001).]||||reg||1
